# Routing, auth guards & client state

**Applies to:** `src/routes/**`, `src/store/**`, `src/hooks/**`

- **Routing:** React Router v6 via `createBrowserRouter` in `src/routes/router.tsx`. Routes are nested
  under layout routes, use `lazy()` + `Suspense` for heavy screens, set the tab title via
  `handle.title`, and cross-fade with `viewTransition`. Centralise paths in `routes/paths.ts` — don't
  hard-code route strings.
- **Guards:** wrap protected routes in `ProtectedRoute`; role-gated routes in `RoleRoute`. Don't roll
  per-component auth checks.
- **Client/UI state = Zustand** (`store/authStore`, `progressStore`, `uiStore`). **Server state stays
  in TanStack Query** — don't mirror fetched data into Zustand.
- **Auth/permissions:** read auth from `useAuth`/`authStore`; gate UI with `usePermissions().can(...)`
  against the permission map — don't check raw roles inline.
- **Session UX:** idle-timeout via `useIdleTimeout`; the app boots unauthenticated and restores via
  `GET /auth/me`.
- **No secrets/tokens in `localStorage`.** Auth is an httpOnly cookie; persist only non-sensitive UI
  prefs if needed.
